    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d257">

                <pb facs="0409" n="315" xml:id="pg315"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">815.001 T 63/-: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The President’s Personal Representative in
                        Honduras</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Welles</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tegucigalpa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-04-30T09:00:00-06:00"><hi rendition="#italic">April 30,
                                1924—9 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received May 1—1:45
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>15. General Tosta will take office at 10 a.m. today as Provisional President. His
                    election and the provisions of the preliminary pact as signed at Amapala on
                    April 28 have now been definitely accepted by all elements. A state of peace
                    obtains throughout the Republic.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Welles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
